   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. I did not run it through a parser, so validity is checked by hand only.\n\n**Left tricycle.** A 2-hydroxyphenyl group sits on a pyridazine ring. The pyridazine is fused to a pyrazine ring that carries an NH and a CH2, and that pyrazine is fused to a piperazine. The piperazine nitrogen farthest from the pyridazine is acylated.\n\n**Stereocentre of the tricycle.** The ring-fusion CH has a wedge to the CH2\u2013NH carbon. The hydrogen is therefore at the back. The CIP priorities are ring N, then the CH2 on the amide-N side, then the CH2\u2013NH, then H. Traced on the drawing, these go counterclockwise, so the centre is S. In the SMILES order written, `[C@H]` gives S.\n\n**Linker.** The carbonyl joins to a 2-methylpiperazine through the N next to the methyl-bearing carbon. The methyl is drawn on a wedge, so H is at the back. The priorities are N1, then the CH2 leading to N4, then CH3, then H. Traced on the drawing, these go counterclockwise, so the centre is S. In the SMILES order written, `[C@@H]` gives S.\n\n**Right-hand end.** The other piperazine nitrogen carries a CH2 that leads to the 4-position of a piperidine. The piperidine nitrogen is bonded to C6 of an isoindolin-1-one. The lactam nitrogen of the isoindolinone carries a glutarimide (2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl). That glutarimide carbon is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc2c(nn1)NC[C@H]1CN(C(=O)N3CCN(CC4CCN(CC4)c4ccc5c(c4)C(=O)N(C4CCC(=O)NC4=O)C5)C[C@@H]3C)CCN21"
